reframeT -- forms step 6, stroke 1 (SEQ 626 W1): setFrame takes a request holding form:=, lays out a COPY and returns it; the
form's definition is never written. Six shapes (the six of docs/setFrameProbes/secondRun.sh), each printed before, laid out
twice, and printed after. Rows in genLadder/pop.sh: the definition reads the same before and after (and still says 50%);
the second run's frames equal the first's; down=3 gives 6 cells both times, not 18; a request with no form refuses by name.
Stroke 2 (W2): the request may hold frame:= a field of its own with x y width height. pPctWideReq lays pPct (declared 200 wide
at 0,0) out in the frame of pPct400 (400 wide at 10,20): a resize must read like a fresh run of a form declared at that size,
and twice like once, with pPct's definition still reading 200. pPctZeroReq's frame is at 0,0: a zero is a value, not an absence.
pPctShortReq's frame lacks x and y and is refused by name.
Stroke 3 (W3): a parent that names overlay (and neither down nor across) overlays its children: each fills the parent's box unless
it declares its own width, height, x or y, and its x and y are measured from the parent (R4). pOver is that parent. pStack (down)
and pBare (no direction at all) are the controls: both stack, and a child's x and y are not read. R3 as dispatched made pBare overlay
too; it was built so first, and the descriptions form and unitTests' sample moved, because the old GUI's default with no direction
named is down, not overlay (GUI/Details.twk: "or !flexed down = true"). The default is back with Tony.
pDeep is five levels deep: copyOf's copy shares bodies below its second level, so setFrame on it wrote frames into the definition's
own deep fields (found by resizeT, where simple's text kept its first frame after a resize). setFrame copies with copyDeep.
